# Topological assembly for the original93/100 analytic carriers

These are complete topological/index inputs for the original analytic proofs, not a claim that their nonlinear regularity, compactification, bubble classification, exhaustive gluing or naturality is finished. The analytic owner retains those proofs and the necessary fixed-curve representative truth repair in original93. No original Statement is changed here.

## Original93: lem-knot-floer-holomorphic-triangle-transversality-compactness-gluing

Use the actual finite balanced Morse construction in `lem-heegaard-polygon-spin-c-difference-is-the-capped-periodic-domain`, with all intermediate marked points retained. It assigns the actual triangle Spin-c structure, restricts to the actual Morse corner labels, and identifies the difference of two same-corner classes by jPD of their capped domain difference. Thus at one fixed Spin-c structure and the fixed entire mark vector, all domain differences lie in the actual sum of normalized adjacent pair-periodic lattices. This is a necessity statement for actual continuous classes, not a quotient of genus-two classes or a domain/class bijection.

For a triple, strong admissibility means the strict OS8.8 condition on this normalized sum lattice: a nonzero P with the sum of restricted Chern evaluations 2N>=0 has a coefficient strictly greater than N. The pair version is exactly the corrected target Definition. `lem-heegaard-polygon-relative-maslov-variation-is-chern-plus-marks` identifies the actual physical relative Fredholm index with that Chern sum plus twice the sum of ALL w-degree changes. Its proof includes the signed actual incidence calculation for periodic strips, actual realization of pair domains in symmetric degree at least two, the degree-one cancelling-Morse-pair comparison, and the common-cap operator index theorem. It does not import a general-Y formula from an S3-only supplier.

Now `lem-strong-polygon-admissibility-bounds-indices-and-positive-domains` gives finite nonnegative DOMAIN sets in every upper index band, and a finite lower index bound, even before regularity. In particular this applies to triangles of fixed indices0/1 and to the finite parameter columns used for universal index−1/0 spaces; actual parameter columns add their ordinary finite-dimensional index. Every pair-periodic restriction lattice is contained in the triple lattice, so the same strict condition supplies the lower bounds for the end-strip sectors. The analytic proof may use these finite domains for its energy and compactness bounds across ALL literal classes. It must still prove the stated regularity, precise compactification, bubble/decomposition exclusions and exhaustive nonlinear gluing; none follows from counting domains. Under actual polygon gluing the Spin-c labels form the proved H1-seam extension orbit, rather than a chosen unique extension. A supplied continuous family and an actual neck smoothing preserve its total Spin-c extension, and all w/z marked vectors add across the face. Capped-Spin5.1 supplies actual collar extension of each attaching-system isotopy, its full Spin lift including torsion, disk-prism transport of capped classes and Chern functionals, and unchanged old-region strict witnesses. Analytic map transport and curve-genericization remain the analytic owner’s separate constructions.

## Original100: lem-os-disk-and-polygon-analytic-foundations

The same actual constructions work for arbitrary closed oriented three-manifolds and every finite number of polygon edges, with balanced symmetric degree h+k−1. They provide the fixed-Spin-c/orbit determinant index formula and strict-admissibility domain bounds, including genus one/two and point-target exceptions, once the actual counted classes and their Spin-c labels are specified. This is the appropriate input to any fixed-Spin-c surgery or continuation operation. It neither defines a nonexistent translation quotient on a stable triangle nor counts positive-dimensional spaces.

For a hat polygon operation that sums over ALL Spin-c labels, use instead the separate global zero-mark hypothesis of `lem-strong-polygon-admissibility-bounds-indices-and-positive-domains`: every nonzero formal MULTI-periodic domain with all marks zero has both signs. It gives finite nonnegative zero-mark domains without fixing a label or index. Pairwise weak admissibility and one fixed Spin-c strong-admissibility condition are not substituted for this global hypothesis. The original link-surgery construction must supply its actual operative multi-diagrams with whichever global admissibility condition its all-label counts require; that construction is not established by this topology bridge.

For a supplied pair sector with actual strips, the separate realized-subgroup branch proves finite domains at fixed entire mark vector and finitely many indices under the literal realized normalized index-zero weak predicate, including symmetric degree one. It supplies no move invariance or nonempty generator set in a previously empty intended sector. The empty-generator full-module Definition defect and the ordinary-sector move comparison remain the grid owner’s separate necessary interface correction and construction. In particular no unproved three-interval triangle gluing is used to promote a formal genus-one pair period to a realized disk.

The original100 analytic conclusion still requires its actual universal-domain regularity, compactness, all codimension-one boundary classifications, degeneration cancellations and exhaustive gluing. The present bridge supplies labels, domain differences and the physical index/finiteness inputs; it does not assert those remaining analytic conclusions.
